# LF everywhere, on every platform.
#
# This repo's own emitted config carries `@stylistic/linebreak-style: unix`, so LF
# is the stance it takes for the projects it governs; taking a different one for
# its own tree would be odd. But the reason this file exists is narrower and
# sharper: `fixtures/adoption/**` are byte-exact test inputs.
#
# On Windows, git's default `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites them at checkout. An
# assertion like `expect(read('CLAUDE.md')).toBe('@AGENTS.md\n')` — which proves
# blueprint left a hand-written file ALONE — then fails against '@AGENTS.md\r\n',
# comparing not what blueprint wrote but what git changed on the way in. The
# fixture stops being a fixture.
#
# This does NOT mean CRLF input is out of scope: an adopter's own tsconfig on
# Windows is very often CRLF, and reading one is a real requirement. That case is
# covered by tests that build CRLF text explicitly, where the line ending is the
# subject rather than an accident of checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish assets, left untouched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
